codemap 9
tour feature-save
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Ctrl+s or the save button in the top bar writes the map to .codemap/, one file per tour, writing only the files whose text changed and deleting the files of removed tours. The reader needs it because edits made in the window live only in memory, and would be lost on close or overwritten by a reload. The button reads 'save *' while there are unsaved changes. A map that could not be read at startup is never saved over. After a save, the reload that the file watcher would trigger is suppressed because the stored stamp matches.

